  <releases>
    <release version="26.8.3" date="2026-08-18">
      <description translate="yes">
        <p>Packaging only: the Android build now produces identical output on any machine, so F-Droid can verify it against this source. Nothing changes in the app itself.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="26.8.2" date="2026-08-18">
      <description translate="yes">
        <p>Fixes for entering a session length by keyboard on Android, and a packaging change so F-Droid can verify the app against its source.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Android: typing a duration and tapping Set now keeps what you typed, instead of falling back to the previous value</li>
          <li>Android: tapping the hours or minutes selects the whole number, so the first keystroke replaces it</li>
          <li>Android: the dismiss button in the session editor is announced as "Cancel" by screen readers again</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="26.8.1" date="2026-08-17">
      <description translate="yes">
        <p>Same as 26.8.0, with a packaging fix so F-Droid can rebuild and verify the Android app.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="26.8.0" date="2026-08-17">
      <description translate="yes">
        <p>A longer reach for daily goals, and a friendlier way to set a session length on Android.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The daily goal can now be set to anything up to 24 hours, instead of stopping at 4</li>
          <li>Android: tap the hours or minutes in the time picker to type a duration, rather than only stepping it with the plus and minus buttons</li>
          <li>Android: the Save button in the session editor no longer runs off the edge of the screen in languages with longer words</li>
          <li>Android builds are now reproducible, so the published APK can be verified against this source</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="26.7.1" date="2026-07-20">
      <description>
        <p>Nextcloud sync between all your devices, a guided-audio mode, daily goals, custom sounds and vibration patterns — and the first release of the Android companion app.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Sync sessions, labels, presets, bells, and preferences between your devices via your own Nextcloud server — offline-first, with automatic conflict handling and remote-storage compaction</li>
          <li>New Guided mode: import your own guided-meditation audio; the end bell rings when the track finishes</li>
          <li>Stats now track a daily goal: the progress ring resets each day and the heatmap stars days that cleared it</li>
          <li>Interval, starting, and end bells are configurable per mode, with imported custom sounds and a visual vibration-pattern editor</li>
          <li>Session log gains CSV export/import (duplicate-safe on re-import) and Insight Timer import</li>
          <li>Duplicate labels created on two devices can be merged from a conflict prompt, moving all sessions onto the surviving label</li>
          <li>Android companion app (F-Droid): the same modes, log, stats, and sync, sharing the identical core — plus a home-screen widget for one-tap preset starts, in all ten languages</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>

    <release version="26.4.4" date="2026-04-24">
      <description>
        <p>A new Box Breath timer mode, per-label stats, and an in-app diagnostics view for bug reporting — plus a handful of polish fixes.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>New Box Breath mode alongside Countdown and Stopwatch: pick a pattern (4-4-4-4, 4-7-8-0, 5-5-5-5) or dial in each phase, set a session length, and the running view traces a dot around an accent-tinted square as you breathe in, hold, out, hold</li>
          <li>Stats tab shows a "By label" breakdown below the streak / total / sessions row, so you can see how much meditation time you've spent under each label</li>
          <li>About dialog has a new Troubleshooting view with a rolling diagnostics log (startup, database open, import/export results, panics) — copy or save to attach to a bug report</li>
          <li>Each timer mode remembers its own last-chosen label, so a Box Breath session no longer changes the default label for Countdown or Stopwatch</li>
          <li>Release notes shown in the About dialog now reflect the current version instead of staying pinned to the initial release</li>
          <li>Log-edit calendar picker shows the proper icon again; post-session note field no longer steals focus on phones and hides the Save / Discard buttons behind the on-screen keyboard</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>

    <release version="26.4.3.1" date="2026-04-21">
      <description>
        <p>Performance and polish pass, focused on Linux phones like the Librem 5. The app starts and switches views noticeably faster on lower-end ARM hardware, and the consequential-action buttons now carry the standard red tint.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Cold start is roughly twice as fast on slow ARM phones; view switches, session start, and session end no longer stall the UI</li>
          <li>Haptic feedback on session end now fires correctly on devices with feedbackd, without the end-sound doubling up</li>
          <li>Stop, Discard, and per-session delete buttons are styled as destructive (red) per the GNOME HIG</li>
          <li>Log view loads 15 sessions per page by default instead of 200, with Load more for older entries</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>

    <release version="26.4.2" date="2026-04-21">
      <description>
        <p>Major polish release ahead of Flathub submission — every tab redesigned, new data features, and translations in nine languages.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Timer, Stats, and Log tabs fully redesigned around the GNOME HIG</li>
          <li>Stats now shows a weekly-goal ring, a 13-week contribution heatmap, and an insights panel</li>
          <li>Log is a date-grouped card feed with swipe-to-delete and undo</li>
          <li>CSV import and export, plus one-click migration from Insight Timer</li>
          <li>Real CC0 recordings replace the three built-in end sounds, with Singing bowl as the new default</li>
          <li>Post-session note field is now multi-line</li>
          <li>Weekly goal resets on the locale's first day of the week</li>
          <li>New "Vibrate on session end" toggle for Linux phones</li>
          <li>Full translation coverage across English, German, Spanish, French, Italian, Dutch, Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, Russian, and Simplified Chinese</li>
          <li>Adaptive layout down to 360 px; HIG-compliant accent colours and accessibility</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="26.4.1" date="2026-04-13">
      <description>
        <p>Initial release.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>

  <supports>
    <control>pointing</control>
    <control>keyboard</control>
    <control>touch</control>
  </supports>

  <requires>
    <display_length compare="ge">360</display_length>
  </requires>
</component>
